Gates — third-party notices
===========================

`LICENSE` (MIT, © 2026 MoreRight DAO) covers **the code in this repository**.
It does not, and cannot, cover everything in the tree: some of what ships is
somebody else's work carried under its own terms, and several of those terms
are *notice* licences — the credit IS the condition, so a missing line here is
a licence breach rather than a cosmetic gap.

This file is the credit. `CLAUDE.md` §"Third-party credit" is the working
record behind it and is where a new entry gets argued; this is the copy that
travels with a build.


What ships, and under what
--------------------------

**game-icons.net icons** — CC BY 3.0 Unported.
**64 of the 65** white-on-transparent PNGs in `assets/icons/`, rasterised from
the project's public SVG archive by `ci/bake_icons.py`. The four authors whose
work ships are **lorc**, **delapouite**, **carl-olsen** and **john-redman**.
The 65th, `burnt_meat.png`, is ours (authored in `ci/icons/`) and **this CC BY
notice does not cover it** — the split is stated rather than inferred, and
`assets/icons/CREDITS.md` keeps the two in separate tables for that reason.
Full per-file mapping and the licence URL are in that file, which ships beside
the icons. `crates/client/tests/ui.rs` §G fails if it stops travelling or if
the baked set and `ui::icons::STEMS` drift apart.
https://game-icons.net · https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/

**Roboto Condensed** — Apache-2.0, © 2011 Google Inc.
`crates/client/fonts/RobotoCondensed-{Regular,Bold}.ttf`, compiled into the
client binary with `include_bytes!`. The notice that must travel with them is
`crates/client/fonts/LICENSE-ROBOTO.txt`; `crates/client/tests/ui.rs` §F fails
if it stops travelling.

**bevy_procedural_tree** — MIT OR Apache-2.0.
A dependency whose code ships: the native client's conifer generator.
It is `@dgreenheck/ez-tree`'s algorithm (MIT, © Daniel Greenheck) ported to
Rust and Bevy. https://github.com/Affinator/bevy_procedural_tree

**Quaternius — Universal Animation Library** — CC0 1.0.
`assets/models/mannequin.gltf` + `.bin`. CC0 asks for nothing; recorded here
because a reader auditing the tree should not have to re-derive it.
https://quaternius.com/

**Generated 3D assets** — commissioned output, not licensed work.
Meshes under `assets/models/` produced with Meshy carry rights from a vendor
contract rather than a licence. `assets/models/MANIFEST.md` records vendor,
mode, prompt, task id and date for each one, which is what makes the rule
auditable after the fact rather than a promise.

**MinGW-w64 runtime** — *Windows builds only.*
`libstdc++-6.dll` and `libgcc_s_seh-1.dll` — GCC, GPLv3 with the
**GCC Runtime Library Exception** 3.1 — and `libwinpthread-1.dll` (winpthreads,
MIT/Expat with BSD-3-clause and public-domain parts, © 2011–2016 the mingw-w64
project). Reached through `basis-universal-sys`, Bevy's KTX2/Basis transcoder.
They ride beside `gates.exe` in the Windows depot because Windows does not
provide them and the build cannot start without them; the notice that must
travel with them is `LICENSE-MINGW-RUNTIME.txt`, staged into every Windows
depot by `ci/depot.py`, which refuses to package one without it.
**The Runtime Library Exception is what the "nothing derives from GPL work"
line below relies on** for these two files: it permits conveying the runtime
alongside output of an unmodified GCC, so no part of Gates' own source becomes
subject to the GPL. Stated rather than assumed, because it is the single place
in this tree where a GPL-licensed artifact ships.

**Rust dependencies.** Everything else linked into these binaries comes from
crates.io and carries its own licence, overwhelmingly MIT OR Apache-2.0.
`Cargo.lock` is the exact list for any given build; `cargo about` or
`cargo deny` will render it if a full manifest is ever required.


What does NOT ship, and therefore owes nothing here
---------------------------------------------------

Recorded because "we read it" and "we shipped it" are different facts, and the
distinction is the whole of this repo's IP posture:

- **`.claude/skills/threejs-*`** — the Three.js graphics skill pack, MIT,
  © 2026 Scott Sun. Guidance only; no code from the pack is in this repo.
- **`reference/rust-systems.txt`** — facts (hook names, class names,
  signatures, categories) extracted from OxideMod/Oxide.Rust (MIT,
  © 2013–2020 Oxide Team and Contributors). Carbon.Hooks (GPL-3.0) is cited as
  a coverage cross-check and deliberately never extracted from, so nothing
  committed here derives from GPL work. Nothing in `reference/` ships.
- **SeedThree**, **Eanpa-Sky** (both MIT, © 2026 SkyeShark) and
  **Claude-of-Duty** (MIT, © 2026 mshumer) — read for technique. No code from
  any of them ships. Their audio is out of bounds on separate grounds: the
  bird recordings are CC BY-NC-SA or licence-unstated, and neither survives a
  sold product — which is why `crates/client/src/sound/synth.rs` generates the
  bank at boot instead.

**`crates/client/src/scry_overlay.rs`** is elo's SDK vendored byte-for-byte —
same author, same licence, so no notice is owed. It is listed here only so
that a reader who finds an unfamiliar file does not go looking for a missing
credit.


Nothing here is traced from Rust (Facepunch)
--------------------------------------------

No proper noun and no asset of theirs is in this repository. Where a number or
a technique of theirs is used, it is cited as a measurement in `reference/`,
which is a fact about a target rather than a copy of a work.

**This became true on 2026-08-11, and had been false before that** — recorded
here rather than quietly corrected, because the sentence above is the kind a
reader is entitled to check. Eighteen screenshots of their game were carried in
`Rust Images/` from the first commits: the evidence base `ART.md` measures the
visual bar off. They were never packaged into a release build, but this
repository is public, and hosting them here was redistribution regardless of
what was shipped. They were removed; `ART.md` §0 states the posture and holds
the measurements, which are statistics rather than images and stay. Anyone
re-deriving the bar points `GATES_REFERENCE_DIR` at their own copy.

The general rule the removal encodes: **a measurement off a work may live here;
the work may not.**
